= Conclusion

System-One Control Bench distinguishes choosing a good isolated move from completing a game. Full context improves Jev's won rate and nearly eliminates its repeated blocked moves, yet strong exam performance does not ensure a completed route. Longer sequences have mixed effects. Jev's moves with chosen probability $p >= 0.9$ are more often optimal (0.74 versus 0.42 below; H7 in @tab:hyp), although the reliability curve is not monotone. These results concern the evaluated puzzles, representations and inference settings.
